+---
+title: Targeted Block
+description: Display personalized content to specific customer segments, groups, or cart rules using Targeted Blocks.
+sidebar:
+  label: Targeted Block
+---
+
+import TableWrapper from '@components/TableWrapper.astro';
+import Link from '@components/Link.astro';
+import Diagram from '@components/Diagram.astro';
+import Vocabulary from '@components/Vocabulary.astro';
+import OptionsTable from '@components/OptionsTable.astro';
+
+Display personalized content to customers based on their customer group, segment, or active cart rules. Targeted Blocks enable you to show different promotions, messaging, or content to different customer types without creating separate pages.
+
+<div style="background-color: var(--sl-color-blue-low); border-left: 4px solid var(--sl-color-blue); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 0.25rem; margin: 1rem 0;">
+<strong>Boilerplate version: 4.0.1</strong>
+</div>
+
+## Vocabulary
+
+<Vocabulary>
+
+### Targeted Block
+
+A block that wraps content targeted for specific customer groups, segments, or cart rules.
+
+### Group
+
+(<Link href="https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/commerce-admin/customers/customer-groups" text="Adobe Commerce Customer Group" />) assigned to the customer.
+
+### Segment
+
+(<Link href="https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/commerce-admin/customers/segments/customer-segments" text="Adobe Commerce Customer Segment" />) that applies to the customer.
+
+### Cart Rule
+
+(<Link href="https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/commerce-admin/marketing/promotions/cart-rules/price-rules-cart" text="Adobe Commerce Cart Price Rule" />) that applies to the customer cart.
+
+</Vocabulary>
+
+## Document authoring configuration
+
+Targeted Blocks accept the following parameters to control which customers see the content:
+
+<OptionsTable
+  compact
+  options={[
+    ['Parameter', 'Description'],
+    ['Customer Groups', 'Comma-separated list of customer group IDs that determine which customers can view the block.'],
+    ['Customer Segments', 'Comma-separated list of customer segment IDs that determine which customers can view the block.'],
+    ['Cart Rules', 'Comma-separated list of cart rule IDs that determine which customers can view the block.'],
+    ['Fragment', 'The path to the fragment containing the content.'],
+    ['Type', 'The type of block to use for the fallback chain creation. Only the first block that satisfies the conditions of each type is displayed.'],
+  ]}
+/>
+
+If the fragment is not used for a Targeted Block, the last merged row of the block configuration must contain the content.
+
+## Section metadata
+
+Control the section styling that wraps your commerce block using the section metadata table:
+
+<table style="width: 100%; min-width: 470px; max-width: 100%; table-layout: fixed; border-collapse: collapse;">
+<tbody>
+<tr>
+<td colspan="2" style="text-align: center; padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5); background-color: var(--sl-color-gray-6); font-weight: 600;">section-metadata</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td style="width: 50%; padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);">Style</td>
+<td style="width: 50%; padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);"><em style="color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); font-style: italic;">light, highlight <span style="font-size: 0.85em;">(optional)</span></em></td>
+</tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<div style="background-color: var(--sl-color-blue-low); border-left: 4px solid var(--sl-color-blue); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 0.25rem; margin: 1rem 0 2rem 0;">
+<strong>Learn more:</strong> See the <a href="/merchants/quick-start/section-metadata/">Section Metadata guide</a> for complete styling options and the <a href="/merchants/quick-start/page-metadata/">Page Metadata guide</a> for SEO, caching, and social sharing options.
+</div>
+
+## Usage examples
+
+### Target specific customer segments
+
+Specify comma-separated customer segment IDs from Adobe Commerce to ensure the block displays only for customers matching these segments.
+
+The content in this example displays only to customers in segments 1 and 2:
+
+<Diagram caption="Targeted Block for specific customer segments">![Targeted Block for specific customer segments](@images/dropins/personalization/targeted-block.png)</Diagram>
+
+### Load content from a fragment
+
+Instead of embedding content directly in the Targeted Block, specify a path to a fragment. The system loads content from the specified document path and displays it as the Targeted Block content.
+
+This example loads content from the document path specified in the fragment property:
+
+<Diagram caption="Targeted Block loading interactive content from a fragment">![Targeted Block loading interactive content from a fragment](@images/dropins/personalization/targeted-block-fragment.png)</Diagram>
+
+### Create fallback content using block type
+
+When multiple Targeted Blocks on a page share the same type, only the first matching Targeted Block displays to the customer. This fallback behavior enables you to configure a Targeted Block with default content visible to everyone, which specific blocks for particular groups or segments can then replace.
+
+In this example, the first Targeted Block displays only to customers whose shopping cart meets the conditions of cart price rule ID 5. The second Targeted Block has no conditions and should display to all customers. However, because both blocks share the same "Type" value, the second block will not display when the first block is active. Blocks with the same type replace each other in the display hierarchy:
+
+<Diagram caption="Targeted Block fallback using block type">![Targeted Block fallback using block type](@images/dropins/personalization/targeted-block-type.png)</Diagram>
+
+## Tips for merchants
+
+- Test Targeted Blocks by switching between different customer groups in your storefront
+- Use fragments for complex interactive content that needs to be reused across pages
+- Create default content with no targeting rules as fallback for customers who don't match any segments
+- Use the Type parameter to create layered fallback chains for progressive personalization
+
+## Related resources
+
+- <Link href="https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/commerce-admin/customers/customer-groups" text="Customer Groups (Adobe Commerce)" />
+- <Link href="https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/commerce-admin/customers/segments/customer-segments" text="Customer Segments (Adobe Commerce)" />
+- <Link href="https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/commerce-admin/marketing/promotions/cart-rules/price-rules-cart" text="Cart Price Rules (Adobe Commerce)" />
+- <Link href="https://github.com/hlxsites/aem-boilerplate-commerce" text="Adobe Commerce Boilerplate" />
+
